              "id": "e73fe9d3-f00e-3484-b5e1-67bc6c410d11",
              "name": "High-Risk Vulnerability Detected in Version 3.0.4, Resolved in Versions 3.2.15 and 4.0.7",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nA high-risk vulnerability was detected in Django version 3.0.4. This vulnerability could allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code, potentially taking control of the system. This is a serious security concern as it could lead to unauthorized access and manipulation of data, disruption of service, and other malicious activities.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nThis vulnerability is a security concern because it allows an attacker to exploit the system by executing arbitrary code. This could lead to unauthorized access to sensitive data, disruption of service, and other malicious activities. The attacker could potentially gain full control of the system, which could have severe consequences for the organization.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade Django to version 3.2.15 or 4.0.7, which have resolved this issue. Regularly updating and patching software is a crucial part of maintaining secure systems. It is also recommended to use secure coding practices to prevent such vulnerabilities from occurring in the first place.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nUpgrade your Django version in your requirements.txt file:\n\n```\nDjango==3.2.15\n```\nor\n```\nDjango==4.0.7\n```\n\nThen, update your dependencies:\n\n```\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the Django library to execute properly.\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Code Review Guide](https://owasp.org/www-pdf-archive/OWASP_Code_Review_Guide_v2.pdf)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are active and accessible to anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
              },
