            {
              "id": "c8caa4a7-82a8-3f68-8786-af1c67fe1baa",
              "name": "\"@csrf_exempt Usage Detected Indicating Potential CSRF Token Vulnerability\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `@csrf_exempt` decorator in Django Python framework is used to bypass the Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) protection for a particular view. If this decorator is used without proper caution, it can lead to CSRF vulnerabilities. CSRF is an attack that tricks the victim into submitting a malicious request. It uses the identity and privileges of the victim to perform an undesired function on their behalf.\n\nIn the provided code, the `results` view is exempted from CSRF protection, which means that it can potentially be exploited by CSRF attacks.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid using the `@csrf_exempt` decorator unless it's absolutely necessary. If you must use it, ensure that the view does not perform any state-changing operations or any operations that need to be protected.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nRemove the `@csrf_exempt` decorator from the view:\n\n```python\ndef results(request, question_id):\n    response = \"You're looking at the results of question %s.\"\n    return HttpResponse(response % question_id)\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires Django, a high-level Python Web framework.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP CSRF Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross-Site_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/352.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-352",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/352.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-352"
                ]
              }
