              "id": "32ad4479-f4cd-3e8f-baff-df974a31d043",
              "name": "\"High Severity Vulnerability in Gunicorn Package, Resolved in Version 22.0.0\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe Gunicorn package in Docker, prior to version 22.0.0, has a high severity vulnerability. This vulnerability allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code remotely, potentially compromising the security of the system. This is a serious security concern as it can lead to unauthorized access and control over the system.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nThis vulnerability is a security concern because it allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code remotely. This means that an attacker could potentially gain unauthorized access to the system, manipulate data, or even take control of the system. This could lead to a variety of negative outcomes, including data loss, data theft, and disruption of services.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade the Gunicorn package to version 22.0.0 or later. This can be done by updating the package in the requirements.txt file:\n\n```\ngunicorn==22.0.0\n```\n\nAfter updating the package, it is also recommended to run a security scan to ensure that the vulnerability has been properly mitigated.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo fix the vulnerability in the source code, you should update the version of the Gunicorn package in your requirements.txt file:\n\n```\ngunicorn==22.0.0\n```\n\nThen, you should rebuild your Docker image and redeploy your application.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- Gunicorn version 22.0.0 or later\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top 10 Security Risks](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Code Review Guide](https://owasp.org/www-pdf-archive/OWASP_Code_Review_Guide_v2.pdf)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n\nPlease note that all links have been tested and are active for anonymous users."
              },
