            {
              "id": "38a5a5ae-6bf9-3cee-9a79-8c80017c7173",
              "name": "\"High Severity SQLParse Package Vulnerability (CVE-2024-4340) Resolved in Version 0.5.0\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe High Severity SQLParse Package Vulnerability (CVE-2024-4340) is a critical security flaw found in the SQLParse package version 0.3.1 used in Docker programming language. This vulnerability allows an attacker to execute arbitrary SQL commands via a crafted SQL statement. This is a serious security concern as it can lead to unauthorized access to sensitive data, data corruption, or even system takeover.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nThis vulnerability is a security concern because it allows an attacker to manipulate SQL queries, which can lead to unauthorized access to sensitive data, data corruption, or even system takeover. An attacker can exploit this vulnerability by sending a specially crafted SQL statement that is parsed by the vulnerable SQLParse package. This can lead to a variety of attacks, including SQL Injection, which is a serious security risk.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade the SQLParse package to version 0.5.0 or later, which contains a fix for this vulnerability. It is also recommended to use parameterized queries or prepared statements to prevent SQL Injection attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nUpgrade the SQLParse package to version 0.5.0 or later. You can do this by updating the version in your requirements.txt file:\n\n```python\nsqlparse==0.5.0\n```\n\nThen, run the following command to update the package:\n\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- SQLParse version 0.5.0 or later\n\n## OWASP and CWE Links\n\n- [OWASP SQL Injection Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)"
              },
